  "lemma": "H real symmetric; R real square; sym(R)>0; ||I-RH||_infinity<=Z<1 implies H>0. Invertibility follows. Exact energy coercivity lower bound m=(1-Z)/||R||_infinity.",
  "proof": "A=RH has spectrum Re>0. X=H^-1 solves AX+XA^T=R+R^T. Integrate derivative of exp(-At)X exp(-A^Tt): X=int_0^infinity exp(-At)(R+R^T)exp(-A^Tt)dt>0. Hence H>0. H^-1=(I-(I-RH))^-1 R gives inverse infinity bound and reciprocal spectral-radius coercivity.",
  "counterexample_if_symR_premise_dropped": "H=R=-I has zero contraction defect and negative definite H.",
